[00:34.69]Conversation One
[00:37.03]M: Hello, good afternoon!
[00:39.68]W: Good afternoon, sir! 
[00:41.27]How may I assist you?
[00:42.89]M: Yes, this is my first trip here. 
[00:45.55]I don't want to miss the best moment here. 
[00:48.47]But I have no idea where to go. 
[00:50.98]Can you recommend?
[00:52.37]W: Of course, sir. 
[00:53.70]You may go to Tanah Lot Temple. 
[00:55.61]It's one of the major temples here. 
[00:57.68]Visitors love it. 
[00:58.99]It is set on the rock and circled by the sea water.
[01:01.96]M: OK, tell me about it.
[01:04.38]W: Certainly, sir. 
[01:05.79]It is on the southwest coast of Bali. 
[01:07.96]According to the record, it was built in the 16th century. 
[01:11.45]Before this temple was built, the designer felt the vibration of holiness and spiritual protection. 
[01:17.37]There is a sacred spring there when the sea water recedes. 
[01:21.23]You can also meet the holy snakes there.
[01:23.75]M: The holy snakes? I'm afraid of snakes!
[01:27.86]W: The snakes are believed to be the guardians of the temple. 
[01:30.99]You are safe. 
[01:32.13]The snakes never attack people unless they are disturbed. 
[01:35.32]The view there is very amazing.
[01:37.52]M: Well, can you arrange a tour guide for me?
[01:40.61]W: Sure. When will you go there?
[01:42.65]M: Tomorrow, at 9 o'clock.
[01:45.33]W: Alright, sir. 
[01:46.48]So I will arrange a trip including a tour guide for you for tomorrow.
[01:50.64]M: How much is it?
[01:52.30]W: It is $20 per person including a buffet dinner and you can enjoy the delicious local food at your dinner, which is quite exotic.
[02:00.41]M: Would you tell me more about the food?
[02:03.15]W: Well, you must try Lawar, which is a crunchy-tender mix of vegetables, grated coconut meat and minced meat mixed with various heady herbs and spices. 
[02:13.71]Babiguling or the suckling pig is another famous dish. 
[02:18.15]A lot of Westerners love it. 
[02:20.14]M: I will put that in my notebook later. Thank you.
[02:23.27]W: My pleasure.
[02:26.52]Questions 1 to 4 are based on the conversation you have just heard.
