[03:48.47]Conversation Two
[03:51.57]M: Excuse me, I'm from Side by Side TV channel. 
[03:55.87]Can I have a few minutes for an interview?
[03:58.91]W: Sure, with pleasure!
[04:01.04]M: First of all, congratulations on winning the competition! 
[04:04.85]It was quite an achievement!
[04:07.30]W: Thank you very much.
[04:09.10]M: How do you feel about winning this prestigious dancing competition? 
[04:13.48]I heard that there were lots of excellent competitors from all over the country.
[04:18.08]W: I should say I'm surprised, proud and touched at once.
[04:22.50]M: When was the first time you were interested in dancing and what triggered off your interest?
[04:27.98]W: When I was 5 years old, my mom took me to a live dance show. 
[04:32.05]And I started to love it.
[04:34.02]M: Do you take special dancing courses or do you just do self-learning to sharpen your talent?
[04:39.73]W: Well, I do both of them. 
[04:41.70]I attended some classes to practice the basic dancing skills. 
[04:45.22]At the same time, I watched a lot of videos about various styles of dancing. 
[04:50.33]I also learn from some prominent dancers.
[04:53.37]M: How did those classes train you?
[04:56.02]W: As the students progress, the training focuses on developing strength, flexibility, endurance, discipline and body control demanded by modern and contemporary dance styles. 
[05:07.08]Talented students with potential will receive close guidance and intensive training to prepare them for a professional dancing or teaching career.
[05:15.47]M: Do you also learn about music?
[05:18.00]W: I learn a traditional musical instrument to support my skill. 
[05:21.72]I picked drum which is extremely helpful for me to grasp the essence of beat.
[05:26.49]M: What was the hardest thing in your career? 
[05:29.41]Was it the hard work you had to undertake while training?
[05:32.92]W: Nope. The hardest thing was when I had to convince my parents of my career choice. 
[05:38.01]They were not supportive at the beginning.
[05:40.27]M: How do you feel about dancing?
[05:42.92]W: Dancing is like my soul. 
[05:44.80]I feel completely satisfied by dancing.
[05:47.98]M: Thank you for your time.
[05:51.25]Questions 5 to 8 are based on the conversation you have just heard.
[05:56.10]5. What is this conversation mainly about?
[06:14.23]6. What made the woman love dancing?
[06:31.30]7. Why did the woman pick learning drum?
[06:48.70]8. What is the hardest part in the woman's dancing career?
